0..71 Comment "// Loops and their exits. A `loop` or a `while` may run forever, so the"
72..151 Comment "// function holding one states `Partial` in its row, `-F [Partial] T`: the host"
152..221 Comment "// interface with no operation, which nothing handles. A caller holds"
222..302 Comment "// it in its own row, and an entry runs at `+U (-F [Partial] T)`. A `for` over a"
303..377 Comment "// list descends on the list and needs no entry; each `become` is an exit."
378..380 Comment "//"
381..396 Comment "// - see: #1481"
397..477 Comment "// - see: #283 — `find_succ`, `find_one`, `find_none`, `for_each`, `for_value`"
